                        "entry_id": "8b3901e8-4115-3fce-b5de-2c99e3fb26cd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A temporary lake in an area of limestone, filled by rising groundwater during the rainy winter season."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ireland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b5fbfd4-67ec-4cc4-84c1-0c6b45b841df",
                                "sense_id": "21c91ca3-b70f-316e-8dba-a6f4a1e353cc",
                                "text": "Naisi said that it was a turlough, or a disappearing lake, and that before the year's end, it would be full of water again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec8299e3-0551-4dfc-a382-bb5f75a20548",
                                "sense_id": "21c91ca3-b70f-316e-8dba-a6f4a1e353cc",
                                "text": "How deep was that small lake—more a turlough really, filled with water in autumn and winter, a dry hollow in summer[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
